  "drawings": {
    "sheet": {"size": [17, 11], "margin": 0.4, "title_block_width": 2.3},
    "theme": "white",
    "font": "Liberation Sans, DejaVu Sans, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif",
    "plan_cut_height": 60,
    "scales": ["3\"=1'-0\"", "1-1/2\"=1'-0\"", "1\"=1'-0\"", "3/4\"=1'-0\"", "1/2\"=1'-0\"", "3/8\"=1'-0\"", "1/4\"=1'-0\"", "3/16\"=1'-0\"", "1/8\"=1'-0\""],
    "general_notes": [
      "All dimensions are to framing unless noted. Rough-sawn boards are full dimension; verify actual sizes delivered by the mill and update the stock table before cutting.",
      "All lumber within 6\" of grade, and all skids, rims, joists, posts and bottom plates: pressure treated. Skids UC4B (ground contact).",
      "Fasteners in contact with treated lumber: hot-dip galvanized (ASTM A153) or stainless. Siding: 8d ring-shank HDG, battens: 10d ring-shank HDG nailed through the gap only, so boards can move.",
      "Board-and-batten boards are nailed to horizontal blocking at 24\" max. and to plates. Leave a 1/2\" gap between boards for shrinkage of air-dried lumber.",
      "Locate the pit at least 50' (verify local code; often 100') from any well, spring, stream or lake, and with 2'+ of unsaturated soil between the pit bottom and the seasonal high water table. Confirm with the local health authority.",
      "The pipe is set plumb and level-topped, backfilled with compacted native soil in 6\" lifts. The pit has an open bottom; do not bed it in concrete.",
      "Relocation: remove the back panel, drag the sled from the skid ends (tow holes provided), insert the flange after positioning. See sheet A-502.",
      "Screening structural checks are shown on A-601. This is not a stamped engineered design."
    ]
  }
